{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/37588-interlocks","id":37588,"title":"Interlocks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-26T18:19:22-08:00","id":37588,"title":"Interlocks","content":"before Christmas we had our first demon game, my players love it so I'm planing on making it more long term. Which I didn't want to do because I only have the preview, but as long as it is all going well I'm in.<br /> <br /> I just finished making one of the players Cipher and interlocks and was wondering what everyone's general thought were.<br /> I will not be posting the final secret for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> Cipher:<br /> First Key: living recorder Pg. 211<br /> Second Key: Synthesis, Pg. 199<br /> Third Key: Shatter, Pg. 187<br /> Fourth Key: Identity theft, Pg. 207<br /> <br /> Interlocks:<br /> <br /> Past records: allows a demon to experience past events with in an area. The demon must be present with in the area and the records are experienced in real time. Leaving the demon unaware of what is currently happening around her. The demon must specify an exact time. The farther away the events are the harder they are to retrieve, each day levying a cumulative -1. <br /> Dice pool: Wits + investigation, Cost: 1 Aether, Action: instant.<br /> Dramatic failure: an incorrect or alternate history is experienced by the demon.<br /> Failure: nothing happens.<br /> Success: Works as expected (all or nothing effect).<br /> Exceptional Success: The demon spends half the time experiencing the events. Six hours in the Past records equals three in the current time.<br /> <br /> Breaking point: with this interlock a demon can retroactively shatter an object. This power alters the time line as gently as it can. The demon needs to touch the object and it cannot be anything larger than her size.<br /> Dice pool: Wits + Crafts, Cost: 1 Aether, Action: instant.<br /> Dramatic failure: From the intended breaking point onward the object gathers occult energy. Exploding once the demon uses this interlock on it. Dealing 2L damage for every day spent gathering occult energy. <br /> Failure: nothing happens, and the object remains unchanged.<br /> Success: Each success allows the Demon to reach farther back in time. A stationary object measures successes in days and a moving object measures successes in hours. <br /> Exceptional Success: allows the demon minor manipulations in the objects ret-coned history.<br /> <br /> Identity loss: The Demon can dislocate a person from her identity. The victim completely forgets who they are. All the under pinning concepts of who they were, are lost on them; they don\u2019t recognize their own face let alone their name. Gender, relations, address, nationality are all lost and in addition to all that the victim finds it difficult to except or understand the truth, and always prefers to rationalize that they are nobody. <br /> Dice pool: Manipulation + Subterfuge - resolve, Cost: 1 Aether, Action: instant.<br /> Dramatic failure: the victim gains a subconscious hold on their identity. +3 to resist any compromise of their identity; including but not limited to mind control, manipulation, interrogation, and hallucinations. <br /> Failure: nothing happens<br /> Success: Each success adds to the penalty for the victim to reintegrate back into their life. <br /> Exceptional Success: Successes are their own reward.<br /> <br /> Memory theft: The Demon can pull and upload memories from people, choosing to either leave the memory or erase it from the victim. The demon must either know roughly the memory she wants to take or the time frame of the memory in question. The demon must touch the person <br /> Dice pool: Manipulation + Subterfuge - Resolve, Cost: 1 Aether, Action: instant.<br /> Dramatic failure: The victim\u2019s memory becomes highlighted in their mind turning the details in to an obsession.<br /> Failure: nothing happens.<br /> Success: Each success allows the demon to take about an hour\u2019s worth of memory.<br /> Exceptional Success: Allows the demons fine control over the details she leaves behind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T19:31:21-08:00","id":37611,"title":"","content":"there should be only 3 interlocks, they unlock when you obtain your 2nd, 3rd and 4th key. Also can we know more about the demon in question? It's difficult to judge without knowing more about the demon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T20:10:11-08:00","id":37642,"title":"","content":"I made four interlock purposefully completing the circle, really it's just to make the one key that my player picked more meaningful and hand out an extra power.<br /> <br /> She's a messenger Inquisitor who before the fall was reused as a teacher and muse, made to inspire people. she fell after following through on the orders to convince a student that her thesis was a failure. the student committed suicide and as an angel she become curious of the effects of her message, she fell shortly after that and has begun a quest for the purpose of her mission as an angel. she has met with a demon who is a member of an agency which is after the thesis. through out the game particularly after her fall she has inverted against her messenger incarnation and become about obtaining knowledge rather then delivering it.<br /> Now quite frankly this is a quick synopsis of what was a 5 hour game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T07:55:45-08:00","id":37864,"title":"","content":"I'm not understanding the point of &quot;Breaking Point&quot;. By it retroactively shattering the object, do the effects of that object become undone? So, if used on a gun, what happens to the people shot by that gun in the time covered by this Interlock? And if THIS gun shattered a few hours ago, wouldn't whomever wants a gun have gotten another gun, or used another weapon? What about if someone smashed that gun, could the player use Breaking Point on the remains to undo what was done while the gun was whole? Also, shouldn't anything that mucks with time cause a Compromise roll, at least? Certainly worth it, I'd say, if suddenly you can bring people back from the dead by using this on the weapon that killed them.<br /> <br /> For &quot;Identity Loss&quot;, what's the roll to reintegrate into their lives? What if they keep failing, or with a Dramatic Failure on the reintegration roll? (Plausible, if used on a &quot;normal&quot; human (attributes at 2) and the Demon gets an Exceptional Success) Does doing this obviate the need for Pacts with someone for the Demon to take their Cover Apsects, essentially salvaging things the person's had stripped of them? (That last could be for Exceptional Successes)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T21:09:49-08:00","id":38156,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about how I want uses of breaking point to play out and I've realized that I miss-spoke when I said the object shatters. how it breaks should be relevant and convenient to the situation. also like any other Demon power over use should result in a compromise roll, and over use could come quite quickly depending on what my player has in mind.<br /> <br /> here is a quick example of how i would like it to go: Okay our three Demon PC just leave a building while a sniper awaits on a rooftop down the street. one of our Demons gets shot and goes down potentially dead. Our remaining two take cover and make their way towards the shooter who gets off several more shots; maybe hitting a second character (details become relevant shortly). but in either chase our Demon who knows Breaking Point gets to the buildings stairwell just as our shooter is trying to make his escape. they fight until our Demon touches the sniper rifle and uses Breaking Point.<br /> Now lets say an hour ago the sniper rifle breaks. The path of least resistance means that the shooter dosen't notice, he gets his orders and climbs into position see our three demons leave the building down the street lines up his first killing shot and fires, the gun explodes in his hands. A little detail but clearly an important one.<br /> At this time our demons must have heard the miss fire because they are now making their way towards our gun man, (the reality of it is that by design I would like not to replay much and thus details will be taken for granted.)<br /> Now while the first time there were two of our demons were running towards the shooter now there are three. if the shooter has a second gun, most likely a pistol it isn't like he would have made those pot shots as our demons encroached, and the second demon wouldn't have been hit either. (although if i can digress a little if it were PC on PC violence or i really wanted that second character shot i would only alter the damage done by the difference in the weapons damage.)<br /> and now we are back where we were with reality altered in our favour.<br /> <br /> Now I can only hope it goes as smoothly in game, but that is the design.<br /> <br /> I would say that a lot of Identity Loss victim become mental patients, and hopefully after a lot of therapy and meds (mechanically positive modifiers) they could recover.<br /> <br /> As for the bit about pacts I was thinking that once lost the pieces shouldn't be accessible, as the person can not sign away what they don't have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T13:38:16-08:00","id":38410,"title":"","content":"If you don't like to replay things, why are you handing them a &quot;replay&quot; power?<br /> <br /> What about memories? Does the Demon who uses Breaking Point even remember using it, or do they have both sets of memories? Does the shooter get any resistance to it?<br /> <br /> <br /> And about Identity Loss, I'm not saying they're signed away, more scavenged from reality once the human loses hold of them. Definitely a Breaking Point, not to mention a Compromise Roll, as you literally are stealing their lives. If the person loses their Identity, what about pacts they have already signed? Would be interesting to use this Interlock as a way to undermine other Demons. If used on someone who's part of an Angel's cover, could also be an interesting way to undermine an Angel. And what, pray tell, would it be like if the Demon scavenged (or acquired through a normal Pact) someone's connection with an Angel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T20:25:00-08:00","id":38559,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry I think there is a bit of a disconnect, when i said i don't want to replay things I meant to say that the power dosen't replay events it just changes them and then we pick up have assumed what changes happened. Hopefully a swift and minimal bookkeeping solution.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that the Demon who used the power should remember both and everyone else only remembers the world post change. As for the shooter having resistance, I can't see why or how.<br /> <br /> Identity Loss nullifying pacts is brilliant, but arguably a bit excessive not to mention cruel. Still the I love the spiteful nature of it.<br /> <br /> Could you define what you mean by a person connection to an angel, Like do you mean if a cult leader was receiving visions from an angel and you took over his &quot;cult leader aspect&quot; would you then be the one receiving visions. or do you mean; if an angel posing as a cult leader were to suffer from Identity Loss and you scavenged (something that I'm not sure I will add as a side effect of the power.) their &quot;Cult Leader&quot; aspect or the cover whole-cloth.<br /> In the first case I don't believe supernatural powers transfer, though if the connection was mundane I would allow it but have the angel try to beat you Spoof.<br /> If the seconded I would treat it like angel-jacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T19:59:10-08:00","id":39750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/37588-interlocks?p=37642#post37642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made four interlock purposefully completing the circle, really it's just to make the one key that my player picked more meaningful and hand out an extra power.</div> </div> </div> </div>When do they get the 4th interlock?<br /> First Key: No Interlock,<br /> Second Key: First Interlock + 1 Primum<br /> Third Key: Second Interlock + 1 Primum<br /> Four Key: Third Interlock and Final Secret + 1 Primum<br /> ??? Forth Interlock?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:09:22-08:00","id":40120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>oxinabox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/37588-interlocks?p=39750#post39750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When do they get the 4th interlock?<br /> First Key: No Interlock,<br /> Second Key: First Interlock + 1 Primum<br /> Third Key: Second Interlock + 1 Primum<br /> Four Key: Third Interlock and Final Secret + 1 Primum<br /> ??? Forth Interlock?</div> </div> </div> </div>First and second key = first interlock<br /> Second and third key = seconded interlock<br /> Third and fourth key = third interlock<br /> Fourth and first key = fourth interlock<br /> <br /> completing the circle.<br /> As a little side note because interlock don't ascend in power I'm letting my players complete their circle in either direction and once their circle is complete they get their Cipher","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:15:20-08:00","id":40199,"title":"","content":"But that means ones they unlock there 4th power, they unlock 2 Interlocks (since they can immediately test the 4th key against there 1st), and presumably gain 2 primum, and the Final Secret.<br /> It means the pay off for finding your 4th key, is as great as the pay of for finding the rest combined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T17:42:18-08:00","id":40262,"title":"","content":"Yes, but not necessarily your fourth key (in the circle going clockwise) but always your last key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:21:34-08:00","id":41726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/37588-interlocks?p=38559#post38559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Identity Loss nullifying pacts is brilliant, but arguably a bit excessive not to mention cruel. Still the I love the spiteful nature of it.<br /> <br /> Could you define what you mean by a person connection to an angel, Like do you mean if a cult leader was receiving visions from an angel and you took over his &quot;cult leader aspect&quot; would you then be the one receiving visions. or do you mean; if an angel posing as a cult leader were to suffer from Identity Loss and you scavenged (something that I'm not sure I will add as a side effect of the power.) their &quot;Cult Leader&quot; aspect or the cover whole-cloth.<br /> In the first case I don't believe supernatural powers transfer, though if the connection was mundane I would allow it but have the angel try to beat you Spoof.<br /> If the seconded I would treat it like angel-jacking.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: the Descent, page 24 &quot;Cover&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons have entirely human bodies, fully-detailed backgrounds, relationships, possessions, jobs \u2014 whatever was needed for their Cover. The people \u201crelated\u201d to a demon don\u2019t realize that anything\u2019s wrong. In some cases, they didn\u2019t even exist until he Fell.</div> </div> </div> </div>The people in an Angel's Cover before they Fall are those with connections to an Angel.<br /> <br /> As for transferring supernatural powers, I whole-heartedly think they should be able to be transferred. If someone is getting Psychic visions from a merit they don't realize they have, such as if they aren't able to control or understand them, they should be able to bargain those away (&quot;Take these visions that plague me!&quot;)<br /> <br /> As for using Identity Loss on an Angel, you'd have to contend with their Resistance and Cover, I'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T12:29:01-08:00","id":41868,"title":"","content":"I'd only allow minor supernatural power's to be gain or lost via pact (or identity loss). plagued by visions I've got the cure for that, recently turned into one of the undead try sunlight i hear it does wonders.<br /> <br /> Identity Loss and Memory Theft are both resisted; I didn't write in Cover or Primum but they also apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T23:57:53-08:00","id":46770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/37588-interlocks?p=38559#post38559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry I think there is a bit of a disconnect, when i said i don't want to replay things I meant to say that the power dosen't replay events it just changes them and then we pick up have assumed what changes happened. Hopefully a swift and minimal bookkeeping solution.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that the Demon who used the power should remember both and everyone else only remembers the world post change. As for the shooter having resistance, I can't see why or how.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Idk, Breaking Point is a bit too much of a Get Out of Jail Free card as written. A better interlock might capitalize on the object-reading ability in Synthesis, allowing the Unchained to nudge causality in their favor, imposing penalties based either on successes or Primum on use rolls with the object. Timeline Editting would be more the purview of Shift Consequence, so mixing that Embed with Synthesis would potentially grant finer control, further reach, or both. Of course, Tools for Toys is the best canon power yet if you solely desire a retroactive auto-miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T12:10:16-08:00","id":55601,"title":"","content":"The above-example regarding a &quot;gun being destroyed affecting all subsequent murders with said gun&quot; would only apply to murders in which the crime required EXACTLY THAT GUN. Which ... probably don't exist. Unless someone is specifically using a gun ritualistically (cultist needs to kill someone with said gun, for x reason), subsequent murders would just be done by different guns instead, as the God Machine has rules at work to ensure the causal line remains as close to possible even in light of Demonic interference.<br /> <br /> Or am I missing something?<br /> <br /> And I see what he's saying about the Interlocks going a 4th step. I don't really see a problem with it aside from the ability to game it as someone above pointed out. Cut it down to what it really is: An extra Interlock that your player has half a stake in (since they know their first key is one of their starting powers). But with the Primum and other ancillary benefits of unlocking keys, it's a step far. Though I don't disagree with it in principle, maybe ensure your players know they won't get away with gaming it like that? I dunno. Your game, your rules, boss. xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","user":"64bitjedi","date":". 01-22-2014, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}